{
  "tema": 7264,
  "slug": "ni-siquiera",
  "titulo": "Ni / ni siquiera = not even",
  "subtitulo": "No tenía ni una cobija. Ni siquiera me saludó.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Ni or ni siquiera = not even. After a negative verb: No tenía ni (siquiera) una cobija. At the start, no other negative is needed: Ni siquiera me saludó. Ni is more colloquial; ni siquiera is more emphatic. Also ¡Ni modo! = oh well, no way around it.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "no + verb",
            "+ ni / ni siquiera",
            "+ element"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "ni / ni siquiera",
            "+ element",
            "+ verb (no extra no)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Like other negatives: after the verb you need **no** before; in front, no **no**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Ni** alone is shorter and more casual; **ni siquiera** is fuller."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Very common Mexican set phrases: **ni modo** (_oh well_), **ni loco** (_no way_), **ni de chiste** (_not a chance_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **siquiera** = _even_; **ni** makes it negative."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
